 why:     The parser reached something it did not expect for this construct: Polaron has a
          fixed grammar, so every statement, declaration, and expression has a required
          shape. The token here does not fit it.
 fix:     Compare the line with a working example of the same construct. The usual causes
          are a missing `;` or `}`, a keyword left out (every block needs `{ }`; every
          method a `returns` type), or `{}` used inline where Polaron wants each statement
          on its own line.
